WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.300
The AI strategy meeting.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.127
Everyone wants AI in the product, and they're all looking at you.

3
00:00:06.127 --> 00:00:07.267
Here's how to answer.

4
00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.033
Leadership wants AI in the product this quarter.

5
00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:13.333
A VP saw a competitor's demo.

6
00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:15.733
A PM has six feature ideas.

7
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.300
And the CTO worries about cost and data privacy.

8
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.067
The whole move is to ask questions before proposing anything.

9
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.633
Ask what a win looks like in ninety days.

10
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:31.800
Ask which pain shows up in support tickets, and what data exists and where it can go.

11
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.444
And ask how tolerant customers are of wrong answers.

12
00:00:35.444 --> 00:00:37.567
AI becomes a means, not the goal.

13
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.600
Now choose among the six, scoring each out loud.

14
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.142
Value: does it remove measured pain?

15
00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:46.633
Support ticket volume is cheap evidence.

16
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:53.700
Tolerance for error: summarizing an internal doc is fine, auto replying about refunds is dangerous.

17
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.133
Data readiness: if expertise lives only in heads, it's a content project first.

18
00:00:59.433 --> 00:01:02.400
Measurability: otherwise it gets killed on vibes.

19
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.467
Then commit to something concrete.

20
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:08.867
One internal facing feature, in six to eight weeks.

21
00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:12.100
Shipped with evals and a cost dashboard from day one.

22
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.033
Plus the platform pieces it forces you to build.

23
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:18.467
So features two through six take weeks instead of quarters.

24
00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.467
Address the CTO unprompted.

25
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.633
Offer data residency options.

26
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:26.200
Redact personal data before it leaves.

27
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.367
Cap cost per feature at the gateway.

28
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:29.933
And keep an audit trail.

29
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.233
Be willing to say the unpopular thing.

30
00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:37.600
If an idea needs only a search filter or rule engine, say so.

31
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.867
Nothing builds credibility faster.

32
00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:41.895
Let's recap.

33
00:01:41.895 --> 00:01:44.033
Ask questions before proposing.

34
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:48.433
Score ideas on value, error tolerance, data, and measurability.

35
00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:51.633
Commit to one internal feature plus the platform.

36
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.785
And be willing to say no AI.

37
00:01:53.785 --> 00:01:56.167
Next up: how long all of this takes.
